From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: shell item property handlers, property lists, array stores, BHID_DataObject on arrays, IFileOperation properties

shell32: shell item property handlers, property lists, array property stores,
BHID_DataObject on arrays, IFileOperation::SetProperties/ApplyProperties*

IShellItem2::GetPropertyStore(GPS_READWRITE) returns the property handler
registered for the file's extension (propsys PSGetItemPropertyHandler); a file
with no handler gives STG_E_ACCESSDENIED as before. Read stores merge the
handler's properties under the item's own names and attributes, and honour
GPS_FASTPROPERTIESONLY and GPS_HANDLERPROPERTIESONLY.

IShellItem2::GetPropertyDescriptionList(PKEY_PropList_*) reads the registered
property list of the item's type (ProgID, extension, SystemFileAssociations,
perceived type, * / AllFilesystemObjects, Directory / Folder) and builds the
description list. IShellItemArray::GetPropertyStore returns a store of the
properties all items share (a value only when every item has the same one;
writes go to every item, Commit commits every item); GetPropertyDescriptionList
returns the properties every item's list has; BindToHandler binds
BHID_DataObject and BHID_SFUIObject for several items (a single item is the
item's own).

IFileOperation::SetProperties keeps the change array; operations queued after it
(copy, move, new item) apply it to their result, ApplyPropertiesToItem(s) queue
the application, all at PerformOperations. A failure is the operation's error.
